The Swift pin is bumped from 6.4.2 to 6.4.3, but nothing has been built, tested or landed yet. No build runner picked up the job in three tries over about 45 minutes, so this run ends waiting on that build.

**On main:**
- `3550cb16` sets `SWIFT_VERSION=6.4.3` in both `images/base.Dockerfile` and `images/build.Dockerfile`, changed together as the comment in those files asks.
- `58b3a650` updates the Swift version in `STATE.md`, in a commit of its own.

**Patch release:** main is already on 2.7 and has taken features since `v2.6.1`, so I did not tag `v2.6.2` on main. `release/2.6` pins the same 6.4.2, so I opened backport pull request #948 against it. Its description says to cut `v2.6.14` (or the next free `v2.6.x`) once it merges. Four other backports to that branch are open and also name `v2.6.14`. The 2.2–2.5 release branches pin Swift 6.1.3 on purpose and are left alone.

**Not verified:**
- The build of `58b3a65` (the docs and images gates) is still queued: https://gitlab.com/tacplus-dev/build/-/pipelines/3097248374
- The change has no test of its own, since it only bumps a pin. The image smoke check prints `swift --version` but does not compare it to the pin.
- No service handlers were touched, so the trace propagation rule doesn't apply.

**Left for the next run**, which starts once that build finishes (at most 6 hours):
1. On a green build, queue the land.
2. After the manager's verdict, confirm the rebuilt `base` and `build` images report Swift 6.4.3 on amd64 and arm64, and run the full gates on the new build image.
3. Comment on the issue with the results and close it.
